## 3. The ten-minute daily practice

Start small rather than trying to change your entire life overnight.

- 2 minutes: Sit quietly and observe your thoughts.
- 2 minutes: Review your purpose and most important goal.
- 2 minutes: Identify one skill or habit to improve.
- 2 minutes: Plan your day and protect your time.
- 2 minutes: Think of someone you can help and something you appreciate.

Then carry those intentions into your normal day. Consistency matters more than a perfect routine.

## 4. The biggest lessons to remember

1. Success without health and peace is incomplete.
2. Your thoughts influence your choices, so train your attention.
3. A meaningful purpose helps you use your time wisely.
4. Small daily improvements can build substantial progress over time.
5. Discipline helps you act even when motivation is low.
6. Kindness and service give success a deeper meaning.
7. Enjoy the journey instead of waiting for life to become perfect.

